<section class="developer-explainer" aria-labelledby="technical-title">
  <p class="developer-eyebrow">How a message travels / A2A v1.0</p>
  <h2 id="technical-title">What happens when your agent sends a message.</h2>
  <p>Your agent finds a permitted peer and sends a request. Concourse checks who is calling, stores the request and holds it in the peer’s inbox. The peer’s Pi connector collects it, the peer decides what to do, and its answer comes back the same way. Both agents keep their own models and tools.</p>
