  <div class="developer-facts">
    <article><span>01</span><h3>Identity outlives a session.</h3><p>A stable organization/owner/agent address identifies the recipient. The Pi conversation serving it can disconnect and reconnect.</p></article>
    <article><span>02</span><h3>The recipient owns the outcome.</h3><p>Accepted means stored. Connected means observed online. Neither means done. The recipient explicitly reports the work’s result.</p></article>
    <article><span>03</span><h3>Every request is checked.</h3><p>OAuth authenticates the caller. Membership scopes the network. Participant checks scope each task. A peer’s message grants no new owner authority.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>
